\DOC empty_ss

\TYPE {empty_ss : simpset}

\SYNOPSIS
Simpset with no rewrites, conversions or congruences.

\DESCRIBE
In their maximal generality, simplification operations in HOL Light (as invoked
by {SIMP_TAC}) are controlled by a `simpset'. The simpset {empty_ss} has no
rewrites or conversions at all, and its only prover is {satisfy_prover}, which
allows variables in the conditions of conditional rewrites to be instantiated
from the context. It is used by {PURE_SIMP_CONV} and friends.

\FAILURE
Not applicable.

\SEEALSO
basic_convs, basic_rewrites, basic_ss, PURE_SIMP_CONV, satisfy_prover,
SIMP_CONV, SIMP_RULE, SIMP_TAC.

\ENDDOC
